Five cases in `crates/reflow2-mcp/src/shared.rs`, module `tests::reelect`, pinning the DECISION rather than the plumbing.

🛑 OBSERVED FAILING FIRST, against a stub of today's behaviour: **3 failed, 2 passed**. The two that passed are the counterweights — same build attaches, unknown attaches — which is the correct reading, because today's behaviour is right for those and wrong for the three real cases. That split is stronger evidence than an all-red run: it shows the tests discriminate rather than merely rejecting the stub.

WHAT IS PINNED:
① a DIFFERENT BUILD OF THE SAME VERSION is replaced — the case that cost this session six cycles and that a version check cannot see;
② an IN-PLACE UPGRADE is replaced — Alex's case; `install -m 755` keeps the inode, so this is also the case that refuted the inode proposal;
③ a daemon with NO FINGERPRINT is replaced — it predates the field, which is every daemon alive when this ships;
④ the SAME BUILD is attached to — without this the fix would kill a healthy daemon on every attach;
⑤ an UNKNOWABLE local build attaches rather than guessing.

⚠️ WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER: the SIGTERM and re-election themselves. Those spawn processes and are exercised only by the live path, so the failure mode they carry — stopping a daemon another session is mid-write against — is argued in the capability and not tested here.
